\taxon{Remark}
\title{Separating horizon, cache, and estimator effects}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{transfer-limit}
\tag{open-question}

\p{Prefix Sliding is useful as a named intervention for retained context and
test-time scaling, but its reported configurations do not establish a
universal runtime law, gradient theorem, support expansion, or capability
acquisition. The next questions are to measure horizon, cache, estimator, and
evaluation effects separately, while preserving the controls in
\ref{ftip-00DU}.}

\p{The finite conclusions depend on the declared protocols. They do not
describe a full optimizer or establish a result for all language models.}
